# port-patches.sh: glm/r8b @ cf4dde927470 over glm/zig-engine-fixes-on-186 @ e027c49cd06d (commits 3155e0ea134a..f190863a4e08); regenerate with scripts/port-patches.sh, do not edit
glm_cuda: read TENSORFOLD_NUCLEUS_UNION so top_p draws stop falling back to whole-shard sorts

From MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold#228 (patch 0024 there), by Hector Isaza (hecisaza), applied
on this branch unchanged apart from where it sits beside TF_GLM_NUCLEUS_RACE. The union coverage test was ported but
Sampler.union_cover never set: Engine.init reads it, the ranks agree on it at start (error.NucleusUnionMismatch), and
the 16,384-candidate retry is planned only with a top_p cut or a min_p floor.

Credits: Hector Isaza.
Apply from the checkout root with: git apply 0035-zig-glm-nucleus-union.patch

